data.content:
## What breaks: Sync I/O on the Cosmos DB provider is **fully removed** in EF Core 11

In .NET 10, you had a sync-over-async opt-in. In EF Core 11, **that opt-in no longer exists** — all synchronous calls (`ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`, `SaveChanges()`) **always throw**, regardless of configuration.

### Fix: convert every method to async

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key points:**
- There is **no workaround** — sync APIs unconditionally throw
- All callers up the chain must also become `async`/`await`
- `Add()` itself is fine (it's in-memory); only I/O methods like `SaveChanges` need the async switch

Also watch for the **owned collections** change: empty Cosmos owned collections now return an empty collection instead of `null`, so update any `is null` checks to `.Count == 0`.
